      "content" : [
        {
          "anchor" : "discussion",
          "level" : 2,
          "text" : "Discussion",
          "type" : "heading"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "If the decoder’s current state matches the given key, the decoder advances past the key and its value separator (",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "code" : ":",
              "type" : "codeVoice"
            },
            {
              "text" : ") so that the decoder is in a state where it can decode the value for that key.",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "anchor" : "Performance-considerations",
          "level" : 2,
          "text" : "Performance considerations",
          "type" : "heading"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "If the key you’re checking for is only 3 bytes or only 7 bytes, it’s faster to include the trailing string delimiter (",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "code" : "\"",
              "type" : "codeVoice"
            },
            {
              "text" : ") in the key so that it fully fills a 4 byte value or 8 byte value.",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "If the key you’re checking for is only 6 bytes, it’s faster to include both the leading and trailing string delimiters (",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "code" : "\"",
              "type" : "codeVoice"
            },
            {
              "text" : ") in the key so that it fully fills a 8 byte value.",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : " ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : "To include the ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "inlineContent" : [
                {
                  "text" : "leading",
                  "type" : "text"
                }
              ],
              "type" : "emphasis"
            },
            {
              "text" : " string delimiter you’ll need to specify a ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "code" : "-1",
              "type" : "codeVoice"
            },
            {
              "text" : " byte offset, because the decoder will have already advanced just past the leading string delimiter after calling ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "code" : "advanceToNextKey",
              "type" : "codeVoice"
            },
            {
              "text" : ".",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
